---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_217",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 217,
  "text": "[[855.9]] <b>179.  De calculo irrepetibilium [März bis April 1687 (?)]</b>\n [[855.10]] <tab/>[März bis April 1687 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[855.15]] Si idem ponitur et detrahitur, quicquid inde in alio constituitur coincidit <i>Nihilo</i>, seu\n[[855.16]] <i>A</i> (quotiescunque ponitur in aliqua re constituenda) ─ <i>A</i> (quotiescunque detrahitur in\n[[855.17]] eadem) ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Nih.</i> seu ^#6+<i>A</i> + <i>A</i> + <i>A</i> etc.^#6- ─ ^#6+<i>A</i> + <i>A</i> + <i>A</i> etc.^#6- ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Nih.</i> </p>\n<p> [[855.18]] Schol. hoc est <i>A</i> ─ <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Nih.</i>, si non amplius adsit <i>A</i>, in re de qua agitur constituenda;\n[[855.19]] vel ^#6+<i>A</i> + <i>A</i>^#6- ─ <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Nih.</i>, si bis adsit in toto posito et semel in toto detrahendo; vel\n[[855.20]] <i>A</i> ─ ^#6+<i>A</i> + <i>A^#6-</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Nih.</i> si contra. Et ita porro quia per Axioma praecedens pluribus <i>A</i> unum\n[[855.21]] coincidit. </p>\n<p> [[855.22]] Problema aliquam rem ita constituere ex pluribus, ut pro eodem in ea expresse\n[[855.23]] posito et detracto, non liceat substituere <i>Nihil</i>. </p>\n<p> [[856.1]] Si a coincidentibus detrahantur coincidentia, residua sunt coincidentia. Si <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>L</i> et\n[[856.2]] <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>M</i> erit <i>A</i> ─ <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>L</i> ─ <i>M</i>. Nam <i>A</i> ─ <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> ─ <i>B</i> (patet per se) et in posteriori pro <i>A</i>\n[[856.3]] substituendo <i>L</i>, et pro <i>B</i> substituendo [<i>M</i>], (ex definitione coincidentium) fit\n[[856.4]] <i>A</i> ─ <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>L</i> ─ <i>M</i>. Quod erat demonstrandum. </p>\n<p> [[856.5]] Si <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> ─ <i>M</i> ─ <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>P</i>, et <i>N</i> cum <i>A</i>, itemque <i>N</i> cum <i>M</i> sit incommunicans, erit\n[[856.6]] <i>A</i> ─ <i>M</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>P</i>. </p>\n<p> [[856.7]] Expressa ejusdem positio et detractio in aliquo constituendo se mutuo destruunt, si\n[[856.8]] nulla adsit tacita. </p>\n<p> [[856.9]] Nam in <i>P</i> nihil aliud extra <i>N</i> ponitur quam <i>A</i>. Ergo quicquid in <i>P</i> extra <i>N</i> poni tacite\n[[856.10]] debet id poni debet in <i>A</i>; ergo et si id quod est in <i>N</i> extra <i>N</i> tacite ponitur in <i>A</i> poni debet,\n[[856.11]] quod est contra Hypothesin. Posuimus enim [<i>bricht ab</i>] </p>\n<p> [[856.12]] <b>Compensationem</b> voco, si idem ponitur et detrahitur, eamque <b>expressam</b> si\n[[856.13]] expresse quod in alio exprim<angle bracket>endum</angle bracket>. </p>\n<p> [[856.14]] Ex compensatione expressa sequitur destructio tum demum, si nihil sit in destruendo,\n[[856.15]] quod tacite repetitum constitutionem ingrediatur extra compensationem, aut si\n[[856.16]] praecise id omne compensationis, quod extra eam praecise tantum repetitur tam in\n[[856.17]] positione quam detractione repetatur seu <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> ─ <i>M</i> ─ <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> ─ <i>M</i>, si nihil sit in <i>N</i>, quod\n[[856.18]] sit etiam in <i>A</i> aut in <i>M</i>. Ita enim + <i>N</i> expressum, vel quod in ipso est, erit quotiescunque\n[[856.19]] hic ponitur; et ─ <i>N</i> expressum, vel quod in ipso est, erit quotiescunque hic detrahitur.\n[[856.20]] (Nam ex hypothesi praeter <i>A</i> et <i>M</i> nihil extra <i>N</i> adest.) Ergo per axioma 2 <i>N</i> ─ <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Nihil</i>.\n[[857.1]] Sed in casu communicationis constructio non est tuta. Nam ponamus <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ─ <i>B</i> ─ <i>P</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>F</i>\n[[857.2]] ut quod habeant <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> commune sit <i>M</i>, seu sit <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i>, et <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>N</i> + <i>M</i>, quae <i>Q</i>, <i>M</i>, <i>N</i>,\n[[857.3]] <i>P</i> nihil habent amplius commune, alioqui ulterius essent resolvenda. His positis nego pro\n[[857.4]] supra dicto scribi posse <i>A</i> ─ <i>P</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>F</i>. Nam explicando <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> per valores dictos, fiet:\n [[857.5]] <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i> + <i>N</i> + <i>M</i> ─ <i>M</i> ─ <i>N</i> ─ <i>P</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>F</i> hoc est (per Axioma 2) <i>Q</i> ─ <i>P</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>F</i>. Ergo falsum est\n[[857.6]] <i>A</i> ─ <i>P</i> seu <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i> ─ <i>P</i> esse ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>F</i>. Similis erit demonstratio si non <i>A</i> et <i>B</i>, sed <i>B</i> et <i>P</i> aliquid\n[[857.7]] commune habeant; vel si <i>A</i> et <i>B</i>, itemque <i>B</i> et <i>P</i> aliquid commune habeant, nisi contingat,\n[[857.8]] ut quod ipsis <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> commune etiam sit ipsis <i>B</i> et [<i>P</i>] commune quo posito succedet\n[[857.9]] constructio, ut ostendet resolutio, nam sit <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> ─ <i>B</i> ─ <i>P</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>F</i>, et <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i>, et\n[[857.10]] <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>N</i> + <i>M</i>, et <i>P</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>H</i> + <i>M</i>, dico fore <i>F</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> ─ <i>P</i>. Nam resolvendo <i>A</i>, <i>B</i>, <i>P</i>, fiet\n [[857.11]] <i>F</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i> + <i>N</i> + <i>M</i> ─ <i>N</i> ─ <i>M</i> ─ <i>H</i> ─ <i>M</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> (per axioma 2.) <i>Q</i> ─ <i>H</i>, quod ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> ─ <i>P</i>, seu\n[[857.12]] <i>Q</i> + <i>M</i> ─ <i>H</i> ─ <i>M</i>. Verum quando ignoratur [<i>bricht ab</i>]\n [[857.13]] <i>A</i> <tab/>+ <i>B</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> + <i>C</i>\n [[857.14]] <tab/><picture>8010</picture>\n [[857.15]] <tab/><i>A</i> + <i>F</i> </p>\n<p> [[857.16]] In hoc calculo literae <i>A</i>, <i>B</i>, etc. significant certa quaedam irrepetibilia verbi gratia res\n[[857.17]] singulares, item notiones universales, unde repetitio est inutilis; item ordinis quoque hic\n[[857.18]] non habetur ratio. </p>\n<p> [[857.19]] Subalternatur calculo de combinationibus in universum ubi non ingreditur Axioma\n[[857.20]] <i>A</i> + <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i>. </p>\n<p> [[857.21]] Si <i>A</i> est in <i>L</i>, erit <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> in <i>L</i> + <i>B</i>. Nam <i>L</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> + <i>N</i>. Jam <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> est in <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> + <i>B</i>. Ergo\n[[857.22]] in <i>L</i> + <i>B</i>. </p>\n<p> [[857.23]] Si <i>A</i> + <i>B</i> est in <i>L</i> + <i>B</i>, <i>A</i> est in <i>L</i>, hoc non sequitur. </p>\n<p> [[857.24]] Si <i>A</i> est in <i>B</i> et <i>B</i> est in <i>A</i> erit <i>A</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i>. Nam si <i>A</i> est in <i>B</i> erit <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i>. Ergo <i>A</i> + <i>N</i>\n[[857.25]] est in <i>A</i>. Ergo <i>N</i> est in <i>A</i>. Ergo <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i>. </p>\n<p> [[858.1]] Probanda haec consequentia: Si <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> est in <i>A</i>, etiam <i>N</i> est in <i>A</i>. Nam si <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> est in\n[[858.2]] <i>A</i>. Erit <i>A</i> + <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> (per propositionem). Ergo <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> (per axioma). Ergo (per\n[[858.3]] propositionem) <i>N</i> est in <i>A</i>. </p>\n<p> [[858.4]] Si <i>A</i> + <i>N</i> est in <i>A</i> etiam <i>N</i> est in <i>A</i>, nam <i>N</i> est in <i>A</i> + <i>N</i>. </p>\n<p> [[858.5]] Datis duobus <i>A</i> et <i>B</i> invenire tertium ab iis diversum <i>C</i>, ut nihilominus <i>A</i> + <i>C</i> et\n[[858.6]] <i>B</i> + <i>C</i> coincidant. Fiat <i>A</i> ^&.Sg <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> (per postulatum 1.) in quo sumatur aliquid, quod neque sit\n[[858.7]] ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>A</i> neque ^&.SE <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> et factum erit quod quaeritur. </p>\n<p> [[858.8]] Hic prius ostendendum est, dato quolibet cujus data sunt aliqua inexistentia inter se\n[[858.9]] diversa, posse haberi aliud a singulis diversum, nempe compositum ex omnibus vel\n[[858.10]] aliquibus. Quod si quis velit aliquid in eo reperiri, ne compositum quidem ex inexistentibus\n[[858.11]] datis, oportet ut inveniat eorum resolutionem, quae cum dari non ponatur non video\n[[858.12]] quomodo haberi possit, nisi habeant aliquid commune ubi detractio adhiberi potest, sed\n[[858.13]] ea non est hujus loci. </p>\n<p> [[858.14]] Ostendendum quod pluribus datis, quae singula inter se diversa, aliquid componi\n[[858.15]] potest ex ipsis a singulis diversum. Posset et doctrina combinationum his conjungi. </p>\n<p> [[858.16]] In additione seu compositione non habetur ratio qualitatis inter res, neque ordinis,\n[[858.17]] sed simpliciter positionis, ut eodem modo ambo considerentur ad unum aliquod constituendum,\n[[858.18]] quod singulis positis aequivalet. </p>\n<p> [[858.19]] Adhibere licebit numeros ut <i>quaternarius</i>, verbi gratia <i>binarius, quaternarius, octonarius</i>. </p>\n<p> [[858.21]] Post definitionem de Continente et contento veniendum est ad definitionem de\n[[858.22]] Subalternante et disparato, seu de iis quorum alterutrum est continens vel contentum. </p>\n<p> [[858.23]] Pro <i>A</i> ^&.Sg <Leibniz special character> <i>B</i> posset simpliciter poni <i>AB</i>. </p>\n<p> [[858.24]] Calculus de continentibus et contentis est species quaedam calculi de combinationibus,\n[[858.25]] quando scil. nec ordinis rerum, nec repetitionis ratio habetur. Itaque praemittenda\n[[858.26]] esset tractatio de variationibus generalis, nisi malimus hanc considerare ut simpliciorem. </p>\n<p> [[858.27]] Hic quae eadem nota designantur sunt coincidentia. </p>\n",
  "number": "179.",
  "title": "De calculo irrepetibilium",
  "date": "[März bis April 1687 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:179. De calculo irrepetibilium [März bis April 1687 (?)] [März bis April 1687 (?)] Si idem ponitur et detrahitur, quicquid inde in alio constituitur coincidit Nihilo, seu A (quotiescunque ponitur in aliqua re constituenda) ─ A (quotiescunque detrahitur in eadem) ^&.SE Nih. seu ^#6+A + A + A etc.^#6-...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>